    "question": {
      ":question/id": "15b0fcaa-9be9-51a9-81e2-0934c0cda9d3",
      ":question/problem": "Determine the number of pivot columns of the matrix $C,$ given by\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & -1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3 & 3 & 10\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, we need to convert $C$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & -1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3 & 3 & 10\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\quad {R}_{2} :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & -1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3 & 3 & 10\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\quad {R}_{3} :={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & -1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $C$ has $3$ pivots, and therefore the number of pivot columns is $3.$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
