      ":question/problem": "Determine the number of pivot columns of the matrix $B,$ given by\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 & 2 & -3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -3 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -8 & 6 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 3 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, we need to convert $B$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 & 2 & -3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -3 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -8 & 6 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 3 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\quad {R}_{3} :={R}_{3}+(2){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 & 2 & -3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -3 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 3 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\quad {R}_{4} :={R}_{4}+(1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 & 2 & -3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -3 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $B$ has $4$ pivots, and therefore the number of pivot columns is $4.$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
